### Interrupt()
- In Java, the interrupt() method is used to send a request to a thread asking it to stop what it's doing, especially if the thread is sleeping, waiting, or doing a long-running task.
public class Test extends Thread 
{
	public void run() 
	{
		try 
		{
			for(int i=1;i <= 5;i++)
			{
				System.out.println("t1 thread running");
				Thread.sleep(3000); // waiting
		    }
		}	
			catch(InterruptedException i) 
			{
		    	System.out.println("t1 thread terminated ..! ");
		    }		
	}
}

import com.learnCoding.ThreadSchedular.Test;

public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Test d = new Test();
		d.start();
		d.interrupt();
	}
}
OUTPUT:-
t1 thread running
t1 thread terminated ..! 
